# 🚨 `js/dist` is NOT ignored, and that is deliberate.
#
# A Flarum extension is installed by composer straight from this repository —
# there is no build step on the target site — so the compiled bundle is part of
# the package, not a build artefact. Ignoring it produced an extension that
# installed cleanly, registered its routes, answered its API, and rendered a
# blank page, because the JavaScript was simply not there.
/js/node_modules
/vendor
